From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: ipq95xx: c-460: leave the QCN9074 radio off

The C-460's QCN9074 on pcie0 is the scan radio and gets no interface by
default. "wifi config" still adds its radio enabled, keeping the world
domain, and every Wi-Fi reload then flips the regulatory domain of the
other three radios (B180 in the port's records): "Failed to set the
requested Country regulatory setting" on all of them, and a 6 GHz
"Timeout while waiting for regulatory update". Disable that radio when
it is first added; a disabled option already set is kept.

A port patch until wifi-scripts skips radios without an enabled
interface; not for upstream.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 .../ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio      | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..9ab5f27
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/ipq95xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/13-arista-c-460-scan-radio
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Arista C-460: the QCN9074 on pcie0 is the scan radio and gets no
+# interface by default. Leave its radio disabled when "wifi config" first
+# adds it: an enabled radio without an enabled interface keeps the world
+# domain ('00') and flips the regulatory domain of the other radios on
+# every reload, until wifi-scripts skips such radios. A disabled option
+# already set, either way, is left alone.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] || exit 0
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+[ "$(board_name)" = arista,c-460 ] || exit 0
+
+case "$(readlink "/sys/class/ieee80211/$DEVICENAME/device")" in
+*/0000:01:00.0)
+	;;
+*)
+	exit 0
+	;;
+esac
+
+for s in $(uci -q show wireless | sed -n 's/^wireless\.\([^.=]*\)=wifi-device$/\1/p'); do
+	case "$(uci -q get "wireless.$s.path")" in
+	*/0000:01:00.0)
+		uci -q get "wireless.$s.disabled" >/dev/null && exit 0
+		uci set "wireless.$s.disabled=1"
+		uci commit wireless
+		;;
+	esac
+done
